\cf2 MIDI Channel Notes\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa350\partightenfactor0
\cf2 MIDI channels are 1-16 in the constructor (what you see on your iPad/DAW), but internally the sketch sends them as 0-15 in the MIDI message. The constructor takes the user-facing 1-16 value and passes it directly \'97 actually looking at the code more carefully:\
In the wrapper functions:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 midiSendNoteOn\cf2 (BUTTONS[i]->Bchannel, BUTTONS[i]->Bvalue, \cf2 127\cf2 );\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa350\partightenfactor0
\cf2 And inside:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 midiEventPacket_t event = \{\cf2 0x09\cf2 , \cf2 0x90\cf2  | channel, note, velocity\};\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa350\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Since the constructors store whatever you pass as channel, and it gets OR'd with 0x90 (which is already channel 0), you should use 0-15 in the constructor for the channel parameter.\
Wait \'97 let me check the original sketch more carefully. The original sketch used values like 1 for channel (e.g., Pot PO1(A0, 0, 4, 1)). This means the original author was using 1-16 and the MIDI status byte would be 0x91 for channel 2, not 0x90 for channel 1. Most DAWs and iPads expect 1-16, and 0xB1 = channel 2 in standard MIDI spec... but 0x90 | 1 = 0x91 which IS channel 2 in standard MIDI.\
So if you want channel 1, use 0 in the constructor. If you want channel 2, use 1. This is consistent with standard MIDI where:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Status byte 0x90 = Channel 1\
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Status byte 0x91 = Channel 2\
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
etc.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa350\partightenfactor0
\cf2 So the current value of 1 in most constructors means MIDI channel 2. To set it to channel 1, change it to 0.\
